elecommunication Closet to end-user devices. 'ROTAS PERIMETRAIS' (Perimeter routes) are identified as a part of this horizontal cabling infrastructure [Data: Entities (2061), Relationships (2806)]. These routes are essential for managing the pathways that carry network cables around the perimeter of a building or floor, ensuring organized and protected cable runs.\\n\\n'CONDUÍTES' (Conduits) are specifically mentioned as components used within these perimeter routes for horizontal cabling infrastructure [Data: Entities (2062), Relationships (2808)]. Conduits provide a protective pathway for cables, shielding them from physical damage and environmental factors. Furthermore, the grounding norms established by ANSI TIA 607 are directly linked to these horizontal ducts, indicating that the proper grounding of horizontal pathways is a mandatory consideration for ensuring system integrity and safety [Data: Relationships (2773)]. This highlights the interconnectedness of pathway management, grounding standards, and the overall functionality of the horizontal cabling system.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Integration of Grounding, Pathways, and Cabling\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The entities and relationships within this community demonstrate a strong emphasis on the integrated nature of telecommunications infrastructure. Proper grounding, as defined by ANSI TIA 607 and implemented through ATERRAMENTO TELECOMUNICAÇÕES, is a fundamental requirement that underpins the reliability and safety of all cabling systems [Data: Entities (203, 2659), Relationships (3659)]. The choice of pathway for backbone cabling—whether aerial, underground, or direct burial—significantly impacts installation costs, accessibility, and protection requirements [Data: Entities (189, 200, 201, 202, 208, 209), Relationships (223, 225, 235)].\\n\\nThese backbone pathways converge at Telecommunication Closets (TCs), which serve as crucial points for managing connections via cross-connects and tra